        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-17T18:20:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Arguably it makes most sense for the shell to be lowest priority, since we want to get the business doe before dealing with the dev user / test environment.\n\nThe \u0027waitms\u0027 command is the odd one out. Should we consider creating a \u0027wdfire\u0027 command instead, which calls \u0027waitms\u0027 on ECOS but does something special (like disabling interrupts) on Zephyr?",
      "parentUuid": "8ffe90d6_0aefa70a",
      "revId": "a13191d58a6666e008e05747fd67dc967d8c5067",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
